{"id": "EUVD-2026-103920", "enisaUuid": "28adb718-b4b3-3c09-b27a-c86d23386bde", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: gyro: adis16136: fix unprotected debugfs reads\n\nThe serial_number file operations are open coded and never call\ndebugfs_file_get(), which debugfs_create_file_unsafe() requires.\ndebugfs_remove_recursive() therefore does not wait for a read in\nprogress, and unbind frees the iio_dev underneath it.\n\nUse debugfs_create_file() instead.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:44:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b62c3944c006cff85dad881ba2948b2f3ef5a626", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d5b0b62e26d7d30e0e16e2d695f2161f7e92a5a5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b53dc6e15aead039bc6a5e08060c96786240c81d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b05e768420352d9051f86c1a1f20f44fa046ba45", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b498df75d6c29aa3e760127ae0f0003df598b53"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fw25-7hvg-9627", "CVE-2026-98666"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "006258d3-0db2-30a9-912f-6bbf9f7422d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "0282772f-ae1b-3ca4-9ee7-970d25f2e0cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9aaea09b4cbdbe1a80ab3fa1a5d32c3ec61fa6e2 <b05e768420352d9051f86c1a1f20f44fa046ba45"}, {"id": "0f3982dd-a2ad-3f40-aad0-98ab373b6568", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "1a54b403-b23b-3f1c-999c-b6f6017562f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "2663fd93-64c4-3a33-89a8-18a5d25234f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "3b645eb9-63b1-3123-9d88-422f1f51dbba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Lin